--- body ---
## Context

Source: "Read the Paper, Write the Code: Agentic Reproduction of
Social-Science Results" (arXiv:2604.21965v1,
https://arxiv.org/html/2604.21965v1). The paper builds a system that
reproduces empirical social-science results from a paper's methods text
plus its original data, with no access to the analysis code (~85% sign
agreement, ~70% statistical equivalence). It benchmarks four agent
scaffolds — Claude Code, Codex CLI, mini-SWE-Agent, OpenCode — across
GPT-5.4, GPT-5.3-Codex, Claude Opus 4.6, GLM-5.

We do not care about the social-science result. We care about the
*harness* the authors built around the agents: the guardrails, the
grading, the trace instrumentation. Several techniques transfer directly
to IDH's verification and audit surfaces; two independently corroborate
work already in flight (trace-doctor, mechanical-first verification).
This ticket is the pillage manifest — analyse each technique, map it to
a concrete IDH surface, and file sub-tickets for the ones worth adopting.

## The seven techniques, mapped to IDH surfaces

1. **Dual-audit guardrail: regex allow/forbid + LLM-rated violations.**
   Their agents run in a sandbox containing only task text, extracted
   methods, output templates, and symlinked data. A two-stage audit then
   (a) regex-scans every file path / URL the agent touched against an
   allow/forbid list, (b) has a cheap model rate each run "clean → severe
   violation". → IDH surface: **verify-adherence**. We already do
   mechanical-first-then-LLM; the net-new idea is an explicit
   *path-access allow/forbid scan* over the agent's tool trace, not just
   a diff-rule check. Strongest single steal.

2. **Hardcoding audit: numeric literals without a computation path.**
   They flag any output number that appears as a literal in the script
   with no code path producing it (memorised, not computed). → IDH
   surface: **maw-audit / test-audit-llm**. This is exactly the
   "toothless test that hardcodes its expected value" failure mode, and
   the detector is mechanical (AST: literal compared against output with
   no upstream computation). Net-new, cheap, high-signal.

3. **Deterministic grading rubric over LLM-judge, aggregated bottom-up.**
   Cell-level A–F by % difference (A <2%, B <20%, … E sign-mismatch,
   F missing), aggregated cell → table → paper, F's excluded. They
   deliberately avoid an LLM judge for the core comparison. → IDH
   surface: **verify-gate**. Corroborates our anti-rubber-stamp stance:
   prefer a deterministic per-criterion verdict aggregated to per-ticket
   over a holistic LLM "looks good". Adopt the *aggregation discipline*
   (criterion → ticket, with an explicit "missing evidence" grade that
   is excluded, not silently passed).

4. **Blinded structured templates force computation, not recall.** Agents
   get the results table as a template of null cells to fill by analysis,
   never the numbers. → IDH surface: **verify-gate evidence rule**. Same
   shape as our "every exit criterion needs commit SHA + file:line, not
   'CI passes'": hand the verifier the criteria as empty cells it must
   fill with located evidence, blind to the author's self-report.

5. **Trace tool-call taxonomy (6 functions): execution, reading,
   navigation, search, writing, other.** They categorise every agent
   tool call and find e.g. "OpenCode GPT-5.4 makes 2× the tool calls,
   most on execution + reading". → IDH surface: **trace-doctor**
   (ticket 0236). Independent corroboration of the census approach;
   their 6-way taxonomy is a ready-made labelling scheme to fold into
   `scripts/trace-stats.py`. Not a new ticket — a note on 0236.

6. **Multi-run stability as a quality metric.** They reran 20 papers 3×
   and report ">80% of tables grade-spread ≤ 1 across runs". → IDH
   surface: **verification determinism**. We could measure /gaze verdict
   spread across reruns of the same PR as a flakiness signal for the
   verification harness itself. Speculative; file only if cheap.

7. **Root-cause attribution taxonomy.** Discrepancies are labelled Agent
   Error / Extractor Error / Original (paper) Error / Missing Data /
   Other. → IDH surface: **skill-doctor + REROLL diagnosis**. A clean
   taxonomy for "why did verify fail": agent misread vs ticket
   underspecified vs missing context vs genuine bug. Adopt as the
   diagnosis vocabulary in REROLL write-ups and skill-doctor clustering.

## Actions

1. Read the paper's methods/appendix sections in full (this manifest is
   built from the abstract + figures via WebFetch — confirm the audit and
   rubric details before building on them).
2. For each technique above, decide ADOPT / NOTE / DROP. Seeds:
   - ADOPT as sub-tickets: #1 (path allow/forbid scan), #2 (hardcoding
     audit detector).
   - NOTE on existing tickets: #3, #4 (verify-gate), #5 (0236).
   - SPECULATIVE: #6, #7 — file only if the design is cheap.
3. File one sub-ticket per ADOPT item, referencing this tracker; edit
   this ticket to list the children.

## Relevant files (IDH surfaces touched)

- `skills/verify-adherence/` — path allow/forbid scan (#1)
- `skills/maw-audit/`, `skills/test-audit-llm/` — hardcoding audit (#2)
- `skills/verify-gate/` — rubric aggregation + blinded evidence (#3, #4)
- `scripts/trace-stats.py` (ticket 0236) — 6-way tool taxonomy (#5)
- `skills/skill-doctor/` — root-cause taxonomy (#7)

## Invariants

- Mechanical-first: every adopted detector must be a deterministic check
  (regex / AST), with the LLM only as a fallback rater — matches both the
  paper's design and IDH's verify-adherence philosophy.
- No new heavy deps; detectors are pure-Python over existing traces/diffs.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Paper methods + audit/rubric appendix read in full and this
      manifest's claims confirmed or corrected
- [ ] Each of the 7 techniques marked ADOPT / NOTE / DROP with a reason
- [ ] Sub-tickets filed for every ADOPT item, listed here as children
- [ ] This tracker stays open until all children close

